{"step_index":1084,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:29:11Z","thinking":"**Reviewing Established Graph Properties**\n\nInitially, `radius_add_one_le_card` showed `GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ Fintype.card V`. Also, `two_le_romanDominationNumber` concluded `2 ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G`. Considering these results, the next step is to explore potential relationships or implications derived from both properties simultaneously.\n\n\n**Analyzing Graph Conditions and Implications**\n\nIf the graph radius is at least 2 and the Roman domination number is less than the number of vertices, then there exists a Roman dominating function with a weight less than the number of vertices. This implies a vertex with value 0 and another with value 2.  Consequently, all vertices with value 0 must be adjacent to a vertex with value 2.\n\nExploring how to bound the radius with `romanWeight f`. Looking at prior proofs related to ball properties.\n\n\n**Bounding the Radius Using Ball Properties**\n\nAssuming a Roman dominating function with a single vertex having value 2 (S = {u}), all vertices not in V1 are within distance 1 of u. The size of V1 is equal to the Roman weight minus 2. This is useful!\n\nHypothesizing that any vertex not in the ball of radius `1 + |V1|` around `u` must be in `V1`. If `ballWithin k u` is not the entire graph, then all remaining vertices must be in V1.\n\n\n**Deducing Eccentricity and Ball Growth**\n\nThe size of `ballWithin k u` must increase by at least 1 at each step if it isn't the entire graph. Since `V \\ ballWithin 1 u` is a subset of V1, each vertex in this set is \"consumed\" by the ball as it grows. The ball will therefore encompass the entire graph after at most $|V_1|$ steps. So the eccentricity of `u` is at most `1 + |V1|`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -u -c '\\nimport networkx as nx\\nimport itertools\\n\\natlas = nx.graph_atlas_g()\\n\\nchecked = 0\\nfound_u_count = 0\\nfor G in atlas:\\n    n = G.number_of_nodes()\\n    if n < 2 or not nx.is_connected(G): continue\\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\\n    for f_tuple in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\\n        f = dict(zip(nodes, f_tuple))\\n        valid = True\\n        for v in nodes:\\n            if f[v] == 0:\\n                if not any(f[u] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)):\\n                    valid = False\\n                    break\\n        if valid:\\n            w = sum(f_tuple)\\n            # check if there exists u in nodes with ecc(u) <= w - 1\\n            # or even u in S (where f(u) == 2)?\\n            eccs = nx.eccentricity(G)\\n            rad = nx.radius(G)\\n            # does there exist any node with ecc <= w - 1?\\n            # since rad = min(ecc), this is literally equivalent to rad <= w - 1!\\n            if rad > w - 1:\\n                print(f\\\"NO! rad={rad}, w={w}\\\")\\n                exit(0)\\n    checked += 1\\nprint(f\\\"Checked {checked} graphs. In 100% of cases, rad <= w - 1!\\\")\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Verifying rad <= w - 1 on atlas\"","toolSummary":"\"Verify rad <= w - 1 on atlas\""}}]}
{"step_index":1085,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"RUNNING","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:29:20Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:29:20+02:00\nTool is running as a background task with task id: f458c9cf-488d-4cd8-8365-7c4e4b16e3f9/task-1085\nTask Description: /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -u -c '\nimport networkx as nx\nimport itertools\n\natlas = nx.graph_atlas_g()\n\nchecked = 0\nfound_u_count = 0\nfor G in atlas:\n    n = G.number_of_nodes()\n    if n < 2 or not nx.is_connected(G): continue\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    for f_tuple in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\n        f = dict(zip(nodes, f_tuple))\n        valid = True\n        for v in nodes:\n            if f[v] == 0:\n                if not any(f[u] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)):\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n        if valid:\n            w = sum(f_tuple)\n            # check if there exists u in nodes with ecc(u) <= w - 1\n            # or even u in S (where f(u) == 2)?\n            eccs = nx.eccentricity(G)\n            rad = nx.radius(G)\n            # does there exist any node with ecc <= w - 1?\n            # since rad = min(ecc), this is literally equivalent to rad <= w - 1!\n            if rad > w - 1:\n                print(f\"NO! rad={rad}, w={w}\")\n                exit(0)\n    checked += 1\nprint(f\"Checked {checked} graphs. In 100% of cases, rad <= w - 1!\")\n'\nTask logs are available at: file:///tmp/agyhome.NWyWnj/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/f458c9cf-488d-4cd8-8365-7c4e4b16e3f9/.system_generated/tasks/task-1085.log\nYOU MUST TAKE ONE OF THE FOLLOWING TWO ACTIONS: A) either proceed to other relevant work (if any) or, B) simply update the user with a short message (that you have launched the command and will wait for it to finish) and end the turn.\n DO NOTHING ELSE."}
