V_2| = 1$ with center $c$: all $v \\in V_0$ are adjacent to $c$, so $\\{c\\} \\cup V_0 \\subseteq \\text{ballWithin}(G, 1, c)$. The complement vertices are in $V_1$ with cardinality $\\le \\text{weight}(f) - 2$. \n<truncated 1654 bytes>\nlies_univ`: Under `HasRadius G`, any stagnant ball equals `Finset.univ`.\n30: 9. `card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ`: Strict growth of ball cardinality at each non-universal step.\n31: 10. `ballWithin_univ_or_card_ge`: Growth lower bound $(k+1) \\le |\\text{ballWithin}(G, k, v)|$ or universal.\n32: 11. `ballWithin_card_pred_eq_univ`: Ball reaches `univ` in at most $|V| - 1$ steps.\n33: 12. `eccentricity_le_card_pred`: Eccentricity of any vertex is $\\le |V| - 1$.\n34: 13. `radius_add_one_le_card`: Fundamental bound $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le |V|$.\n35: 14. `mem_ballWithin_of_walk`: Walk endpoint containment in `ballWithin` by `Walk.concatRec`.\n36: 15. `mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le`: Length-bounded walk endpoint containment.\n37: 16. `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_forall_walk`: Universal reachability from existence of bounded walks.\n38: 17. `card_ballWithin_add`: Bounding multi-step ball cardinality growth from arbitrary base step.\n39: 18. `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add`: Ball reaches `univ` whenever $|V| \\le |\\text{ballWithin}(G, k, v)| + m$.\n40: 19. `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le`: Transitive bound when $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n41: 20. `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`: Weight bound $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$ when no vertex is assigned 2.\n42: 21. `mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj`: 1-step ball contains all adjacent neighbors.\n43: 22. `mem_ballWithin_one_self`: 1-step ball contains the center vertex.\n44: \n45: ## 4. Verification Check Output\n46: Running `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh Challenge_e20263a9.lean`:\n47: ```\n48: LINT: ok\n49: 'radius_le_eccentricity' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n50: 'prove_e20263a9' depends on axioms: [propext, so