{"step_index":1104,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:30:40Z","thinking":"**Assessing theorem dependencies and axioms**\n\nThe file defines two theorems, `prove_e20263a9` and `refute_e20263a9`, both currently using `sorry`. The `check.sh` script reported that `radius_le_eccentricity` depends on `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`, and that the file is LINT-ok, which means all lemmas are accepted. This implies existing lemmas might be relevant to the candidate theorem.\n\n\n**Developing proof strategy for candidate**\n\nThe goal is to prove the candidate theorem by showing that `radius G + 1 ≤ romanDominationNumber G`. Starting with `le_romanDominationNumber G`, the problem reduces to proving `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`, for an arbitrary Roman dominating function `f`. A case split on `Fintype.card V ≤ romanWeight f` seems promising. If `Fintype.card V ≤ romanWeight f`, apply a relevant lemma.\n\nIf the cardinality condition does not hold, then `romanWeight f < Fintype.card V`.  This means that there must be a vertex with value 2 under `f`. A proof by contradiction seems appropriate, using the definition of a Roman dominating function.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -u -c '\\nimport networkx as nx\\nimport itertools\\n\\natlas = nx.graph_atlas_g()\\n\\nchecked = 0\\nfor G in atlas:\\n    n = G.number_of_nodes()\\n    if n < 2 or not nx.is_connected(G): continue\\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\\n    for f_tuple in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\\n        f = dict(zip(nodes, f_tuple))\\n        valid = True\\n        for v in nodes:\\n            if f[v] == 0:\\n                if not any(f[u] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)):\\n                    valid = False\\n                    break\\n        if valid:\\n            w = sum(f_tuple)\\n            # check if there exists c with f(c) == 2 such that ecc(c) <= w - 1\\n            centers_with_2 = [v for v in nodes if f[v] == 2]\\n            if centers_with_2:\\n                # check if ANY center with 2 has ecc <= w - 1\\n                eccs = nx.eccentricity(G)\\n                has_good_c = any(eccs[c] <= w - 1 for c in centers_with_2)\\n                if not has_good_c:\\n                    print(f\\\"No good center with 2! n={n}, edges={list(G.edges())}, f={f_tuple}, w={w}, eccs={eccs}\\\")\\n                    exit(0)\\n    checked += 1\\n\\nprint(f\\\"Checked {checked} graphs. IN 100% OF CASES with f having a 2, THERE IS A 2 WITH ecc(c) <= w - 1!\\\")\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing if center with 2 has ecc <= w - 1\"","toolSummary":"\"Test if center with 2 has ecc <= w - 1\""}}]}
